Chapter: EntryProbe
  cites Works chapter MetalLadder

 Does a payload built the way the A5 sticks are built reach its first
 instruction at all?

 Three A5 flights have returned a green screen and a medium with exactly two
 sectors changed, both of them flash-usb's own. The compiler's own ladder
 cannot see that: its first rung is inside `opening`, and green means nothing
 reached `opening`. This payload has one rung and nothing else, so it
 discriminates the two states the A5 arm folds together -- died in the runtime
 init, or died later.

 It must be built with the SAME cdx-to-pe flags as the A5 payload
 (`-EntryStart -HeapPages 32768`) and compiled `-Uefi`. Change either and it
 stops answering the question it exists for.

 We say:

Section: Entry

 CYAN before anything else, including before the print. `__start` has already
 run by the time this executes, so a green screen here puts the fault in the
 bare-metal runtime init and a cyan one puts it after.

  opening : [Console] Integer = act
    p <- ladder-pass 1 ladder-cyan ladder-red
    print-line-uni ("ENTRYPROBE painted=" & show p & " base=" & show (boot-fb-base 0))
    ladder-hold ladder-cyan
  end
